m","v":"1.467211","d":"double"},{"po":121535,"n":"stringdb::description","v":"Sulfotransferase 1E1; Sulfotransferase that utilizes 3'-phospho-5'-adenylyl sulfate (PAPS) as sulfonate donor to catalyze the sulfate conjugation of estradiol and estrone. Is a key enzyme in estrogen homeostasis, the sulfation of estrogens leads to their inactivation. Also sulfates dehydroepiandrosterone (DHEA), pregnenolone, (24S)-hydroxycholesterol and xenobiotic compounds like ethinylestradiol, equalenin, diethyl stilbesterol and 1-naphthol at significantly lower efficiency. Does not sulfonate cortisol, testosterone and dopamine."},{"po":121535,"n":"tissue::thyroid gland","v":"2.113946","d":"double"},{"po":121535,"n":"display name","v":"SULT1E1"},{"po":121535,"n":"tissue::adrenal gland","v":"2.387559","d":"double"},{"po":121535,"n":"tissue::gall bladder","v":"1.173046","d":"double"},{"po":121535,"n":"log2FoldChange","v":"3.816689413913533","d":"double"},{"po":121535,"n":"stringdb::sequence","v":"MNSELDYYEKFEEVHGILMYKDFVKYWDNVEAFQARPDDLVIATYPKSGTTWVSEIVYMIYKEGDVEKCKEDVIFNRIPFLECRKENLMNGVKQLDEMNSPRIVKTHLPPELLPASFWEKDCKIIYLCRNAKDVAVSFYYFFLMVAGHPNPGSFPEFVEKFMQGQVPYGSWYKHVKSWWEKGKSPRVLFLFYEDLKEDIRKEVIKLIHFLERKPSEELVDRIIHHTSFQEMKNNPSTNYTTLPDEIMNQKLSPFMRKGITGDWKNHFTVALNEKFDKHYEQQMKESTLKFRTEI"},{"po":121535,"n":"tissue::intestine","v":"2.700781","d":"double"},{"po":121535,"n":"stringdb::node color","v":"rgb(117,239,169)"},{"po":121535,"n":"stringdb::database identifier","v":"9606.ENSP00000226444"},{"po":121535,"n":"tissue::blood","v":"2.054626","d":"double"},{"po":121535,"n":"tissue::spleen","v":"4.257068","d":"double"},{"po":121532,"n":"padj","v":"0.0134555232662497","d":"double"},{"po":121532,"n":"stringdb::namespace","v":"stringdb"},{"po":121532,"n":"tissue::urine","v":"0.60206","d":"double"},{"po":121532,"n":"compartment::nucleus","v":"4.236564","d":"double"},{"po":121532,"n":"stringdb::structures","v":["AF-Q8NDP4"],"d":"list_of_string"},{"po":121532,"n":"tissue::saliva","v":"0.545455","d":