3; Component of a Polycomb group (PcG) multiprotein PRC1-like complex, a complex class required to maintain the transcriptionally repressive state of many genes, including Hox genes, throughout development. PcG PRC1 complex acts via chromatin remodeling and modification of histones; it mediates monoubiquitination of histone H2A 'Lys-119', rendering chromatin heritably changed in its expressibility. Within the PRC1-like complex, regulates RNF2 ubiquitin ligase activity. Plays a redundant role with PCGF5 as part of a PRC1- like complex that mediates mon [...] "},{"po":121292,"n":"tissue::thyroid gland","v":"1.695754","d":"double"},{"po":121292,"n":"display name","v":"PCGF3"},{"po":121292,"n":"tissue::adrenal gland","v":"1.757904","d":"double"},{"po":121292,"n":"tissue::gall bladder","v":"1.227029","d":"double"},{"po":121292,"n":"stringdb::sequence","v":"MLTRKIKLWDINAHITCRLCSGYLIDATTVTECLHTFCRSCLVKYLEENNTCPTCRIVIHQSHPLQYIGHDRTMQDIVYKLVPGLQEAEMRKQREFYHKLGMEVPGDIKGETCSAKQHLDSHRNGETKADDSSNKEAAEEKPEEDNDYHRSDEQVSICLECNSSKLRGLKRKWIRCSAQATVLHLKKFIAKKLNLSSFNELDILCNEEILGKDHTLKFVVVTRWRFKKAPLLLHYRPKMDLL"},{"po":121292,"n":"tissue::intestine","v":"2.393246","d":"double"},{"po":121292,"n":"stringdb::database identifier","v":"9606.ENSP00000354724"},{"po":121292,"n":"tissue::blood","v":"1.934872","d":"double"},{"po":121292,"n":"tissue::spleen","v":"1.838905","d":"double"},{"po":121280,"n":"padj","v":"0.003331490842034","d":"double"},{"po":121280,"n":"stringdb::namespace","v":"stringdb"},{"po":121280,"n":"compartment::golgi apparatus","v":"1.290308","d":"double"},{"po":121280,"n":"tissue::urine","v":"1.404834","d":"double"},{"po":121280,"n":"compartment::nucleus","v":"3.200244","d":"double"},{"po":121280,"n":"stringdb::structures","v":["3lq9_A","AF-Q9NX09"],"d":"list_of_string"},{"po":121280,"n":"tissue::saliva","v":"1.690479","d":"double"},{"po":121280,"n":"stringdb::species","v":"Homo sapiens"},{"po":121280,"n":"compartment::peroxisome","v":"1.945801","d":"double"},{"po":121280,"n":