,"n":"@id","v":"stringdb:9606.ENSP00000418525"},{"po":121058,"n":"compartment::endoplasmic reticulum","v":"2.168803","d":"double"},{"po":121058,"n":"stringdb::description","v":"Neprilysin; Thermolysin-like specificity, but is almost confined on acting on polypeptides of up to 30 amino acids. Biologically important in the destruction of opioid peptides such as Met- and Leu-enkephalins by cleavage of a Gly-Phe bond. Able to cleave angiotensin-1, angiotensin-2 and angiotensin 1-9. Involved in the degradation of atrial natriuretic factor (ANF). Displays UV-inducible elastase activity toward skin preelastic and elastic fibers. Belongs to the peptidase M13 family."},{"po":121058,"n":"tissue::thyroid gland","v":"2.32758","d":"double"},{"po":121058,"n":"display name","v":"MME"},{"po":121058,"n":"tissue::adrenal gland","v":"2.4009","d":"double"},{"po":121058,"n":"tissue::gall bladder","v":"2.663214","d":"double"},{"po":121058,"n":"log2FoldChange","v":"1.358388970792552","d":"double"},{"po":121058,"n":"stringdb::sequence","v":""},{"po":121058,"n":"tissue::intestine","v":"3.765331","d":"double"},{"po":121058,"n":"stringdb::node color","v":"rgb(239,169,117)"},{"po":121058,"n":"stringdb::database identifier","v":"9606.ENSP00000418525"},{"po":121058,"n":"tissue::blood","v":"3.73305","d":"double"},{"po":121058,"n":"tissue::spleen","v":"3.117571","d":"double"},{"po":121052,"n":"padj","v":"0.019892666630525","d":"double"},{"po":121052,"n":"stringdb::namespace","v":"stringdb"},{"po":121052,"n":"compartment::golgi apparatus","v":"1.245534","d":"double"},{"po":121052,"n":"tissue::urine","v":"0.970515","d":"double"},{"po":121052,"n":"compartment::nucleus","v":"5.0","d":"double"},{"po":121052,"n":"stringdb::structures","v":["1buo_A","AF-Q05516"],"d":"list_of_string"},{"po":121052,"n":"tissue::saliva","v":"1.929763","d":"double"},{"po":121052,"n":"stringdb::species","v":"Homo sapiens"},{"po":121052,"n":"compartment::peroxisome","v":"1.422314","d":"double"},{"po":121052,"n":"tissue::liver"